# 
# # Global EM WIRP-Style Implied Monetary Policy Pricer
# ### BQuant single-notebook version
# 
# This notebook uses **live Bloomberg curve objects**, constructs discount factors, and calculates **meeting-to-meeting forward overnight rates on the actual central-bank meeting dates**. It then converts each incremental rate change into the number of standard hikes/cuts priced, producing a WIRP-style line + bar view.
# 
# Initial markets:
# - Mexico — `YCSW0583 Index`
# - Chile — `YCSW0193 Index`
# - Colombia — `YCSW0329 Index`
# - Hungary — `YCSW0324 Index`
# - Czech Republic — `YCSW0551 Index`
# - Poland — `YCSW0327 Index`
# - Turkey — `YCSW0522 Index`
# 
# **Important:** Bloomberg does not expose the FWCV arbitrary-date calculation as an obvious BQL data item. This notebook therefore uses Bloomberg curve-object quotes and Bloomberg's published forward-rate identity. Mexico conventions are configured more specifically; the other countries are parameterized and visibly marked for desk validation.


